  "findings": [
    "Queueing defect found in live use: turns were serialized behind a lock, so a Nova turn throttled by Bedrock (~2 min 45 s each, measured between turns 6-10) blocked later scripted turns ('Checking with EVE...'). Fixed inside I4: a turn in progress now makes /api/turn and /api/reset answer 409 at once, and the page disables all controls while a turn runs. Pre-fix hashes: app.py 8516ee59..., index.html 22d0a68f..., test_web.py 237e8baa...",
    "Register resets are not written to evidence/i4 (they appear only as runs/web_* directories: 5 in session 1 = 1 start + 4 resets, matching the 4 turns that start again from the seed). Proposed for I5: a reset record.",
    "Browser voice input reported 'not-allowed' (microphone permission denied for the page in the browser); speech output unaffected; typing works. Not an EVA defect."
  ],
